#, no-wrap
msgid "Using Yii with Swoole"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-swoole.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Swoole](https://www.swoole.com/) is a PHP extension for event-driven, coroutine-based network applications. It\n"
"includes an HTTP server, coroutine APIs, and runtime hooks for common blocking I/O functions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-swoole.md
msgid "Swoole allows Yii request handlers to run as workers. Each worker may handle multiple requests.  Such an operation mode is often called [event loop](using-with-event-loop.md) and allows not re-initializing a framework for each request that improves performance significantly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-swoole.md
msgid "Swoole supports Linux, macOS, Cygwin, and WSL. Install the extension through PECL:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-swoole.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "pecl install swoole\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-swoole.md
msgid "If PECL doesn't enable the extension automatically, add it to your `php.ini`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ini)
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-swoole.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "extension=swoole.so\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-swoole.md
msgid "Check that PHP loads the extension:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-swoole.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "php --ri swoole\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-swoole.md
msgid "The Swoole project also provides a [Docker image](https://github.com/swoole/docker-swoole) and documents source builds with optional features such as OpenSSL, sockets, MySQL, PostgreSQL, and curl hooks."
msgstr ""

